{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/convexpolygonshape2d"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConvexPolygonShape2D","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A 2D convex polygon shape, intended for use in physics. Used internally in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D","isActive":true},{"text":" when it’s in ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/solids","isActive":true},{"text":" mode.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"solid","type":"text"}]},{"text":", which means it detects collisions from objects that are fully inside it, unlike ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" which is hollow. This makes it more suitable for both detection and physics."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Convex decomposition:"}]},{"text":" A concave polygon can be split up into several convex polygons. This allows dynamic physics bodies to have complex concave collisions (at a performance cost) and can be achieved by using several ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D"},{"type":"text","text":" nodes or by using the "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D","type":"reference"},{"text":" node in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CollisionPolygon2D\/BuildMode-swift.enum\/solids","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" mode. To generate a collision polygon from a sprite, select the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Sprite2D","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" node, go to the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sprite2D"}]},{"type":"text","text":" menu that appears above the viewport, and choose "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create Polygon2D Sibling"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Performance:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConvexPolygonShape2D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is faster to check collisions against compared to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/ConcavePolygonShape2D"},{"text":", but it is slower than primitive collision shapes such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/CircleShape2D","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/RectangleShape2D","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". Its use should generally be limited to medium-sized objects that cannot have their collision accurately represented by primitive shapes."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Inherits From","kind":"rela